{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Lift up</b> — Our earlier ones, of blessed memory, said: this is an allusion to bringing the ark into the Holy of Holies; therefore it is written above, 'in the place of His sanctuary,' and this, 'to the gates' — by way of parable. And the reason: that the place where the ark is was established higher than every mountain and lofty, because of the glory that dwells there." "And the reason for 'gates' and 'doors' ['of the world'] — that they are many." "<b>Doors of the world</b> — that they stand forever, because of the glory of the Glory." "<b>King of the glory</b> — that because of Him was the great glory of the House."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:27.332050344Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}